.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-audit - The operator audit log: every operator write, who did it and to whom


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin audit [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the operator audit log, newest first: one row per write an operator made, with
the operator (actor), the account it landed on (target), the resource, and the detail the
gateway recorded with it (the fields changed and the values they replaced, the exposure an
operator acknowledged, the filters of a clear, …).

.PP
What is recorded: accounts (update, activate, deactivate), onboarding requests (create,
update, send, delete), wallets (update, deactivate, reactivate), the operator role
(grant, revoke), a webhook circuit reset, a transaction redrive, a catalogue reload, a
sync-error clear, and write mode switched on and off. A merchant's own writes are not
operator actions and are not here.

.PP
--actor and --target take account ids ('rail0 admin accounts --search …' finds them).
--payment takes the payment's UUID, not its rail0_id: 'rail0 admin trace 0x…' shows a
payment's operator actions from either.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--action\fP=""
	Only this kind of action, e.g. account.deactivate, wallet.deactivate, sync_errors.clear

.PP
\fB--actor\fP=""
	Only actions by this operator (account id)

.PP
\fB--from\fP=""
	Only actions at/after this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for audit

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--payment\fP=""
	Only actions whose detail names this payment (its UUID): a redrive

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--resource-type\fP=""
	Only actions on this kind of resource, e.g. account, wallet, onboarding, webhook

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort by created_at or action (prefix - for descending; default: newest first)

.PP
\fB--target\fP=""
	Only actions that landed on this account (account id)

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	Only actions at/before this ISO-8601 time


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin audit                                   # the latest operator writes
  rail0 admin audit --target 019e748b-…               # everything done to one account
  rail0 admin audit --actor 019f8a3d-… --from 2026-11-26T00:00:00Z
  rail0 admin audit --action account.deactivate --pretty
  rail0 admin audit --resource-type wallet
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP
